What Is the Semiconductor Probe Cards Market?
Semiconductor probe cards are precision-engineered testing interfaces that establish electrical contact between semiconductor wafers and automated test equipment. They enable manufacturers to evaluate the electrical performance and functionality of integrated circuits before individual chips are separated from the wafer.

The market includes MEMS probe cards, vertical probe cards, cantilever probe cards, and other specialized designs. These components are essential to wafer-level testing across logic, memory, flash, and parametric applications. Increasing chip complexity, advanced packaging, and demand for high-bandwidth memory are driving the need for increasingly precise and reliable testing interfaces.

